{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties","id":1414267,"title":"How do you like your Specialties?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-17T14:34:59-07:00","id":1414267,"title":"How do you like your Specialties?","content":"So I'm toying around with building several characters, and re-reading some older (1E) stuff for inspiration and flavor, since 3E has really inspired me to get back on a serious Exalted kick. And I came across a section in Ruins of Rathess that talks about how foraging in the jungles is difficulty X, but that most people aren't going to be ok with eating thumb sized grubs, so large game is difficulty X+2. And it caused me to consider changing Survival - Urban on my former street rat to Survival - Gross But Effective. Because, to be honest, while Urban gives some flavor, the odds of it ever actually coming up once you have a circle is about nil. Someone in the circle will have resources, or the ability to talk the party into a place to stay. But the ability to crawl into a dead Taun-Taun or eat giant cockroaches, or smear myself with yeddim dung might at least be useful. But (while obviously a question for my particular storyteller), I'm curious as to people's preference for Specialties.<br /> <br /> TL;DR - Do you prefer clear mechanical Specialties, like Awareness - Join Battle, Resistance- Environmental Hazards, and Socialize-Guile, or flavorful ones like Melee - Perfectly Balanced Weapons, Socialize - Making it Up as I Go Along, and Brawl - When Really Angry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T16:01:12-07:00","id":1414282,"title":"","content":"Generally I got with specialties that vibe well. &quot;Single enemy&quot;, &quot;tools that I made myself&quot;, &quot;dissing people&quot;. Stuff that encourages a stunt or three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 09-17-2020, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T16:22:23-07:00","id":1414287,"title":"","content":"The only character I've made for 3E (for myself to use in an actual game, as opposed to characters made for other people or as thought-exercises) had/has... Awareness 5 (Join Battle), Craft: Architecture 4 (Masonry), Athletics 5 (Rushes), Earth Dragon Style 5 (Tetsubo), Lore: Heptagram education 5 (The Shogunate).<br /> <br /> Probably not what I'd go for now. I really like the &quot;Survival - Gross But Effective&quot; one, and I'd probably build towards something like that in the future.<br /> <br /> The &quot;problem&quot; is that Dragon-Blooded really need that Specialty. You need to be absolutely sure you're going to get it on the rolls you need it on. Awareness (Join Battle) is probably the single least... <i>aesthetic </i>thing I've ever done in Exalted... but it's also pretty essential to my character. I mean, it wouldn't be if I hadn't made a character who revolved around calling Celestials and House Matriarchs punk-a**-b****es and having the conjones to back it up. The average Terrestrial PC won't need that specific Specialty... but they <b>will need </b>specific Specialties in the Abilities which are core to their concept. Solars and Lunars have a lot more flex for taking things that just seem cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T16:38:22-07:00","id":1414290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414287#post1414287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;problem&quot; is that Dragon-Blooded really need that Specialty. You need to be absolutely sure you're going to get it on the rolls you need it on.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The average Terrestrial PC won't need that specific Specialty... but they <b>will need </b>specific Specialties in the Abilities which are core to their concept. Solars and Lunars have a lot more flex for taking things that just seem cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sort of the problem with some specialties for everyone, particularly combat ones. Picking a pretty much universally applicable one for Dodge, Melee and MA is sort of necessary for everyone, since +1 to defense is kind of a big deal. Commonly opposed rolls like stealth and awareness or larceny also suffer from this a little (or initiative). It is much worse for DB though. Also, really hard for some abilities. Like Single Point or some Crafts or Integrity. Some abilities (Larceny or Performance or Melee) are so broad you can basically get one all the time for the aspect of it you want. But Tailoring or Architecture are harder, if not impossible (as you showed). And sometimes the boring ones just fit. My street rat does have Awareness - Join Battle, because he's twitchy and quick to react. And Awareness - Quick Reactions or -Ready for Trouble don't really fit, because they're basically just for Join Battle anyway. Awareness - Wary might work, but I can see it being overly broad. When is he /not/ wary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-17-2020, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:59:13-07:00","id":1414305,"title":"","content":"It's only a +1 to defense if you're currently sitting at even though, if you've got 3 dex and 4 melee it doesn't do anything for you there, and it's only a +1 die to attack.<br /> <br /> If you want it to apply to join battle try things like &quot;ambushes&quot; or &quot;Creatures of Darkness&quot; or something. Either way, saying you <i>need </i>max stats and a specialty for join battle is quite the stretch most of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414287#post1414287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not what I'd go for now. I really like the &quot;Survival - Gross But Effective&quot; one, and I'd probably build towards something like that in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting thought you've just given me. What about specialties that you can kind of turn on by doing things a particular way? Like Melee (High Flying Acrobatics) so when the random thug decides he wants a piece of you, you just punch him with no specialty, but when you really need it you vault up 12 feet into the air, and backflip into an attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T18:14:35-07:00","id":1414309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414305#post1414305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting thought you've just given me. What about specialties that you can kind of turn on by doing things a particular way? Like Melee (High Flying Acrobatics) so when the random thug decides he wants a piece of you, you just punch him with no specialty, but when you really need it you vault up 12 feet into the air, and backflip into an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I call those sorts of Specialties 'signature' specialties, or WSAV specialities. (After the Sidereal World Shaping Artistic Vision charm that often used behavioral or stylistic triggers to get the most use out of). Things like Brawl - Dirty Fighting or -While Really Angry. On the one hand, they'll apply almost all the time. They really might as well be 'while stunting' a good 90% of the time. On the other hand, most veteran players pick specialties that apply most of the time anyway. You don't see a whole lot of mounted dawns with dodge: Unarmored. Pretty much just martial artist types. I go back and forth on how I feel about them. Generally I play with an experienced group of continuous players I've known for years, and we're pretty good about not invoking stuff like that every time. (And as a ST, sometimes you fight in a Nexus basement and your spec doesn't apply). I don't think it's any worse than Melee - Swords, at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-17-2020, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T20:31:25-07:00","id":1414323,"title":"","content":"Least &quot;boring&quot; specialty I've done so far by a fair margin is Integrity (Virtuous Conduct).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T20:40:27-07:00","id":1414324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414323#post1414323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Least &amp;quot;boring&amp;quot; specialty I've done so far by a fair margin is Integrity (Virtuous Conduct).</div> </div> </div> </div>.. is that a bonus to resolve to keep yourself to virtuous conduct, or against those sorts of intimacies? ;P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T21:00:39-07:00","id":1414327,"title":"","content":"The first one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T21:18:02-07:00","id":1414328,"title":"","content":"I heard that if you get a +3 specialty on all abilities for &quot;Naked&quot; then Venus herself comes down and slaps whoever wrote that charsheet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T01:28:15-07:00","id":1414337,"title":"","content":"I must say I'm not a fan of specialties. There is already a lot of things to track of as an Exalted, specialties makes one more for a mechanical advantage I don't find interesting. If the results were more &quot;qualitative&quot; (you know like games where you have a threshold success to beat and you have advantage you can spend on your success for special effects) I'd probably like them, but at the moment it's just physical and mental space used for an anticlimactic +1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T02:27:53-07:00","id":1414339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414290#post1414290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is sort of the problem with some specialties for everyone, particularly combat ones. Picking a pretty much universally applicable one for Dodge, Melee and MA is sort of necessary for everyone, since +1 to defense is kind of a big deal. Commonly opposed rolls like stealth and awareness or larceny also suffer from this a little (or initiative).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> <br /> Look at the difficulty chart on Page 185. Look at the NPC dice pools starting Page 495.<br /> <br /> Most of the time, you REALLY don't need that extra die. Defence 4 is enough (so long as you're not running with something silly like 2 Soak, and don't mind a bit of dramatic back-and-forth with Initative Shifts and other excitement in your combats).<br /> <br /> And for Stealth... outside of fellow Exalted, a Fair Folk Lorelei has the most dice to oppose Stealth with &quot;Senses 12 dice&quot; (also, I contend Stealth should usually be a flat difficulty and not an opposed roll, unless the opposition is dramatically appropriate). Dex 3 Stealth 3 Solar Excellency and a basic Stunt gives you a <i>significant edge here</i>. <br /> <br /> Ahlat only gets 11 dice. Most things have 5-8 dice. You don't need Dex 5, Stealth 5, Specialty in &quot;When wearing my Sneakers&quot;, Exceptional Dark Cloak, Belt of Shadow Walking, etc.. <br /> <br /> But a Dex 3/Stealth 3 <i>Dragon-Blooded</i> doesn't even break-even with the Lorelei with a Full Excellency + Stunt. They need that Specailty because it adds an extra die and a whole success.<br /> <br /> (A Tyrant Lizard gets an average of something like 9 successes to oppose Stealth, even though they only get five dice, which is better than most Exalted -- certainly better than the Deathknight's 7, but if you rule the Bronze Faction Assassin can full Excellency, she is hitting 10. So... you need a Specialty for T-Rex guard dogs and the deadliest super-spies in Heaven. <br /> <br /> But for conventional guard dogs, sabre-tooth tigers, Elite Guards, mystic Creatures from beyond the world's edge, two-handed sentries, Directional War Gods, Celestial Censors, Immaculate Martial Artists or Experienced Dragon-Blooded, and Guild Princes... 3+3 is enough, 5/5/1 is ridiculous overkill for a Solar, unless Stealth is like, their whole Supernal &quot;thing&quot; and they're playing, not the Mission Impossible character who can break into anywhere, but the Macavity character who literally cannot be caught.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-18-2020, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T03:55:31-07:00","id":1414347,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm somewhere in the middle here. I don't like purely mechanical Specialties. I feel that picks should be something a character would actually be able to express in character, or have expressed about them. &quot;I have trained in many weapons, but the spear is my favorite,&quot; or, &quot;Don't even try it, out pal here can spot a lie from a mile away,&quot; and that sort of thing. At the same time, I want ones that are practical given the mechanics over dropping character resources on overly specific or hard to adjudicate. ..<br /> <br /> To the value of them in general... I've grown to view them as one of those relics that probably doesn't need to be there. I'd way rather see DB dice-caps get something close to the Lunar stunting method than continue to rely on Specialties.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T04:42:09-07:00","id":1414351,"title":"","content":"Sure. And for a Supernal solar it's more a question of theme, than the one extra dice on top of your 10/20 dice roll with a bunch of charms. My Str 5, Ath 5 Ath Supernal doesn't have Athletics - Feats of Strength because I think I'll need it to tip over a wagon. He has it because he is the strongest one there is. And so he can lift one more plate than the other strongest guys. Or throw a Yeddim at someone. A stealth 5 dex 5 character doesn't want to sneak up on Ahlat, he wants to sneak up on Ahlat over a nightingale floor (-2) while injured (-1) when Ahlat knows he's coming (-2). Or hide behind Ahlat in Ahlat's shadow in his house in Yu-Shan for a day. Or do so on the move in combat without much cover (-5). You know, epic stuff for the epic stealth dude.<br /> <br /> My survival 3 - Gross but Effective dude is fine if his spec doesn't apply. He's not hanging his hat on surviving in hell, or turning a tyrant lizard into a pet. He just wants to be more or less able to make his way wherever, and survival 3 does that. The other thing is mostly flavor, but encourages him to act and stunt a certain way, but could provide bonuses.<br /> <br /> If I'm a dex 3 dodge* 3 Eclipse the difference between evasion 3 and 4 seems far different. And like you said, even for a maximum skill DB, a success or static adder is 50% more effective with a specialty. <br /> <br /> Let's take a not-terribly combative dynast. Maybe he went to the Thousand Scales because men don't have enough self control to make good warriors. He's a fantastic bureaucrat, and getting better at politics. He's got dex 3, ma 3 and an Excellency (at least). That's pretty good (I mean, he's still a DB) If he has a spec, his parry is 4/6. If he doesn't, his parry is 3/4. One of these characters has a whole lot more to worry about from two or three Conscripts (literal peasants dragged from their fields) than the other does. That makes a specialty a big deal for him. (He's obviously going to win, in either case). But he's an elite martial artist (by the book's or a mortal's definitions, if not so among the Chosen), and the applicability of his specialty is likely to matter an awful lot more than either of the Solars above.<br /> <br /> * Sidenote: It really kind of bothers me that investing the same amount of skill at specifically not getting stabbed or shot or whatever is no better than the side effect of getting good at punching people or stabbing them (and since there is no medium weapon equivalent for evasion, worse in many cases). But that's an unrelated issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-18-2020, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T05:13:43-07:00","id":1414361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414347#post1414347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the value of them in general... I've grown to view them as one of those relics that probably doesn't need to be there. I'd way rather see DB dice-caps get something close to the Lunar stunting method than continue to rely on Specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that specialties are kind of neither fish nor fowl right now. While they can certainly be useful, it's not like previous editions where you could have Craft 2: Swords +3 for a Hatori Hanzo type character, or Survival 2: Urban +2 for a indigent street kid. <br /> <br /> I debate changing them out for something like Aspects, sometimes. Picking something, and having it apply to all appropriate skills. So if you have a specialty in Swords, you get a melee bonus with swords, a craft bonus to making swords, a bonus to buying swords, hell probably a bonus to talking to the Sword God. But that causes issues with Sidereals and DBs, as well as having all the 'fun' of trying to thread the spectrum of generally useful to overly broad that intimacies already do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T06:08:31-07:00","id":1414369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414347#post1414347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the value of them in general... I've grown to view them as one of those relics that probably doesn't need to be there. I'd way rather see DB dice-caps get something close to the Lunar stunting method than continue to rely on Specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather Deebs just had a cap of (Ability) (or even, sacrilegious to suggest, I know, a straight cap of 5 dice or 3 successes) and more Excellency effects like Brawl: Become the Hammer (normal Excellency, plus Parry Lethal damage unarmed, plus reroll 6s on damage) and Medicine: Master Healer Meditation (normal dice adding Excellency, but gain a non-Charm success if you hit your dice cap). Let Charms be Charms. Have them do stuff.<br /> <br /> The Lunar stunting method works great for Lunars, but it's not a panacea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414351#post1414351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a hard time parsing this... but I'm pretty sure I agree with everything you posted there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T06:56:49-07:00","id":1414381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414347#post1414347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the value of them in general... I've grown to view them as one of those relics that probably doesn't need to be there. I'd way rather see DB dice-caps get something close to the Lunar stunting method than continue to rely on Specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, fuck it, Liminals are Terrestrials too, and they have a (provisional) dice cap of (Attribute + anima), so why not just use (Ability + anima)?<br /> <br /> But the best solution is probably Essence's (Ability) cap that applies to everyone equally. It makes dice pools less unwieldy AND it closes the gap between terrestrials and celestials AND it helps keeping non-Exalted foes relevant? Yes please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T07:12:49-07:00","id":1414385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties#post1414267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...consider changing Survival - Urban on my former street rat to Survival - Gross But Effective. Because, to be honest, while Urban gives some flavor, the odds of it ever actually coming up once you have a circle is about nil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see an urban Survival specialty getting some use tailing people, or enhancing a disguise as a stableboy, or just finding your way around town.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3e page 157</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">tracking, navigation, and handling animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T07:54:45-07:00","id":1414401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414351#post1414351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. And for a Supernal solar it's more a question of theme, than the one extra dice on top of your 10/20 dice roll with a bunch of charms. My Str 5, Ath 5 Ath Supernal doesn't have Athletics - Feats of Strength because I think I'll need it to tip over a wagon. He has it because he is the strongest one there is. And so he can lift one more plate than the other strongest guys. Or throw a Yeddim at someone. A stealth 5 dex 5 character doesn't want to sneak up on Ahlat, he wants to sneak up on Ahlat over a nightingale floor (-2) while injured (-1) when Ahlat knows he's coming (-2). Or hide behind Ahlat in Ahlat's shadow in his house in Yu-Shan for a day. Or do so on the move in combat without much cover (-5). You know, epic stuff for the epic stealth dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>With nothing more than an excellency though? If you\u2019re sneaking up on a directional war god, while wounded, and over a nightingale floor that might be the time to combo Perfect Shadow Stillness with Sound and Scent Banishing Attitude. If you\u2019re sneaking without cover in combat, use Stalking Wolf and Blurred Form Style to completely negate those penalties, and give you even more bonuses besides, like autosuccesses and free initiative. Those aren\u2019t even like, epic Essence 5 Supernal Only charms, only one of them is even Essence 3.<br /> <br /> The actual Stealth guy, the guy who\u2019s super into stealth? On top of his excellency he\u2019s rerolling all non-10 dice, keeping the 10s, ignoring almost any penalty he has, treating her opponent\u2019s 1s as her own 10s, reducing enemy successes by one for every 1 and 2 they roll, and that\u2019s assuming she isn\u2019t using any number of the automatically successful charms that are completely incontestable. If I can get a 99%+ chance to succeed on my stealth attempt against the greatest and most keen sentinels in the world with just my excellency, what\u2019s even the point of all that other stuff?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414351#post1414351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My survival 3 - Gross but Effective dude is fine if his spec doesn't apply. He's not hanging his hat on surviving in hell, or turning a tyrant lizard into a pet. He just wants to be more or less able to make his way wherever, and survival 3 does that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your survival 3 guy can definitely survive in Hell and tame a Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> If I'm a dex 3 dodge* 3 Eclipse the difference between evasion 3 and 4 seems far different. And like you said, even for a maximum skill DB, a success or static adder is 50% more effective with a specialty. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414351#post1414351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let's take a not-terribly combative dynast. Maybe he went to the Thousand Scales because men don't have enough self control to make good warriors. He's a fantastic bureaucrat, and getting better at politics. He's got dex 3, ma 3 and an Excellency (at least). That's pretty good (I mean, he's still a DB) If he has a spec, his parry is 4/6. If he doesn't, his parry is 3/4. One of these characters has a whole lot more to worry about from two or three Conscripts (literal peasants dragged from their fields) than the other does. That makes a specialty a big deal for him. (He's obviously going to win, in either case). But he's an elite martial artist (by the book's or a mortal's definitions, if not so among the Chosen), and the applicability of his specialty is likely to matter an awful lot more than either of the Solars above.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a bit different for DBs, as John pointed out especially for success added charms an applicable specialty can make a pretty big difference, and they also just have less \u201cbasically I just win\u201d charms in their charmset. On the other hand DBs get more specialties than Solars or Lunars, and have charms that grant themselves temporary ones, which helps a bit. I still don\u2019t necessarily think it\u2019s critical to always have an available specialty, especially if you\u2019re already at an even number of of ability dots. It might be a good idea to take multiple specialties in the same ability though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414351#post1414351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Sidenote: It really kind of bothers me that investing the same amount of skill at specifically not getting stabbed or shot or whatever is no better than the side effect of getting good at punching people or stabbing them (and since there is no medium weapon equivalent for evasion, worse in many cases). But that's an unrelated issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the reasoning here is that Dodge is used in more than just combat, it\u2019s also used to resist environmental hazards and disengage, and also the dodge tree tends to be a lot more powerful defensively than brawl/ma or Melee. Although Solar Melee comes close. Also it can be used even while using a bow and against certain unblockable attacks. Although there are also yndogable ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T09:26:57-07:00","id":1414412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414401#post1414401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dodge is used in more than just combat, it\u2019s also used to resist environmental hazards and disengage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your whole comment was useful and thought provoking, but this really triggered something in my mind, since I'm bringing some baggage from previous editions. Given that dodge does multiple things now, would Dodge - Combat Movement and Dodge -Evasion be valid Specialties? I say yes to the first, and viscerally dislike the second, but I'm not really sure it's less valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T09:40:10-07:00","id":1414413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414385#post1414385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an urban Survival specialty getting some use tailing people, or enhancing a disguise as a stableboy, or just finding your way around town.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. I was more concerned with making sure he'd survive being a street urchin to Exalt, but there are a few uses for an Urban Survival spec.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T10:10:48-07:00","id":1414418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414412#post1414412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your whole comment was useful and thought provoking, but this really triggered something in my mind, since I'm bringing some baggage from previous editions. Given that dodge does multiple things now, would Dodge - Combat Movement and Dodge -Evasion be valid Specialties? I say yes to the first, and viscerally dislike the second, but I'm not really sure it's less valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s just a touch too broad, and also just pretty gamey. Either one of those things alone might not be so bad, but they combine to make kind of a bad feeling specialty. Like if you just had a specialty in combat movement that\u2019s a bit gamey, but not so broad.<br /> <br /> Also don\u2019t underestimate environmental hazards. Or, well, maybe do. If you have an inexperienced ST you\u2019ll likely not see them. In my games though you\u2019re very likely to be walking across a frozen mountain lake in the late winter, thaw making the ice slick and giving everyone a -2 penalty to physical actions, and then bam, landslide. Several boulders come hurtling down the mountainside. The guy in heavy armor with no dodge even with Dex 5, has 1 die to make the difficulty 3 Dex+Dodge roll, or else take 5 dice of bashing damage. The guy with light armor and Threshold Warding Stance, even with dex 3 and dodge 2, spends 2 motes and ends up with 5 dice plus one autosuccess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T12:31:19-07:00","id":1414443,"title":"","content":"That's what (as a previous edition player and ST) I'm trying to figure out. Given that Melee - Swords exists, and assuming I want the same breadth in other specialties, does disengage, stand from prone, and environmental hazards happen enough to make me feel like that's a valid spec. (In previous editions that's probably an athletics roll, to avoid the avalanche). I suppose it's basically the same as Melee -Parry, which I would allow but not be particularly fond of, as a ST. I do wish the core book had examples of Specialties for each ability like 1E did. I didn't necessarily love all of them but they gave a solid starting point. IIRC Dodge - With Dodge Charms was one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T12:55:56-07:00","id":1414450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414369#post1414369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let Charms be Charms. Have them do stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not mutually exclusive with the idea that, going all the way back to 1e, DBs could exceed their dice-caps in specific circumstances (which has for three editions been gated via Specialties).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lunar stunting method works great for Lunars, but it's not a panacea. </div> </div> </div>1) I said &quot;close&quot; not &quot;copy.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) It not being a panacea doesn't mean it can't be good approach in this circumstance.<br /> <br /> I understand it's a vague idea I posted off the top of my head and thus doesn't have any specifics to it, thus allowing for imaginations to assume all sorts of horrible implementations. But I'd rather any feedback to at least try to be constructive/productive instead of just, &quot;this is bad because I assume the worst.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414381#post1414381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, fuck it, Liminals are Terrestrials too, and they have a (provisional) dice cap of (Attribute + anima), so why not just use (Ability + anima)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was contemplating using Aura over Anima, but I'm not sure how much I want to hitch anything to the already more-to-track issues of Aura.<br /> <br /> What I like about starting with Aura, is it helps you maintain the idea of DB's going over 5 for their dice-cap as something that's still situationally specific. Like, if you stunt a way to incorporate an Ability from the Aspect you're currently in Aura for, you increase your dice-pool. On a purely aesthetic/thematic level the idea of being in Fire Aura and being able to stunt in Athletics for greater dice-caps while leaping across rooftops and shooting people with a bow, or Water Aura to add Investigation to social attempts from your keen eye for details, etc. is something I find really appealing compared to the current Specialty model or a flat bonus like Anima level.<br /> <br /> There's also probably a way to work teamwork into this somehow, since I like the idea of DBs getting their best stuff as part of a group, but that would need to at least reduce the bonus from +Ability to something lower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the best solution is probably Essence's (Ability) cap that applies to everyone equally. It makes dice pools less unwieldy AND it closes the gap between terrestrials and celestials AND it helps keeping non-Exalted foes relevant? Yes please. </div> </div> </div>I think that's the best solution for Essence and what Essence is trying to do. Maybe Exalted 4e (in the way distant future) will decide Essence should be the way to go for the core-line, but for now, Essence is a side project to make Exalted more accessible to people that struggle with the core-line stuff. I'd rather let the people that like more fiddly bits and power tiers and so on continue to have their fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T14:52:16-07:00","id":1414473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414450#post1414450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'd rather any feedback to at least try to be constructive/productive instead of just, &quot;this is bad because I assume the worst.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said your idea was &quot;bad&quot; or that I &quot;assumed the worst&quot;. So let me cut through it right here: I don't dislike you, and I don't think your ideas are bad.<br /> <br /> I said I'd prefer if DBs could raise their static values by three, or add upto three successes (or five dice, successes counting as two dice) to a roll regardless of their Ability score. I see it as Deebs drawing on a more primal, elemental power -- but one they can't control with the same degree of internalisation and finess as a well trained Solar.<br /> <br /> Mostly, because it's easy to keep track of as ST.<br /> <br /> But you could easily say, I don't know, Stunts raise the DB dice cap by one. Or Stunts that somehow match your Aspect raise caps by one (a Fire Aspect firing a flaming arrow for example). Or Stunts that match your Aura state. Or Bonfire/Iconic Anima raises your cap by 1. Or stunts give +3 dice to DBs (or +4 dice if you're nixing Specialties all together). Or DBs can raise their dicecap to (Attribute+Ability) with a Stunt. Or whatever you want to do with your idea. The reason I like the Stunt thing for Lunars, is that I think it's a great way of mechanically reflecting the Lunar themes of transformation, and adaptibility: they're generalists in a way DBs are not.<br /> <br /> But my idea is just give them a static dice cap of five (or six maybe). And I like my idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414401#post1414401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With nothing more than an excellency though?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those times where you'd think I'd agree with the good Dr, as we're basically making the same point...<br /> <br /> But those Charms have Stealth 5 as a prerequisite, so unless you're going to houserule that away, you might as well grab a Specialty as well and go all-in at that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414412#post1414412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your whole comment was useful and thought provoking, but this really triggered something in my mind, since I'm bringing some baggage from previous editions. Given that dodge does multiple things now, would Dodge - Combat Movement and Dodge -Evasion be valid Specialties? I say yes to the first, and viscerally dislike the second, but I'm not really sure it's less valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodge - Evasion is less valid <i>because of</i> your visceral dislike.<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't a finely tuned machine built to precise tolerances. It's a game of eyeballing things and gut feelings. Trust your viscera.<br /> <br /> (Combat Movement seems fine to me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-19-2020, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T15:57:09-07:00","id":1414663,"title":"","content":"\u201c90% of the time this Ability comes up\u201d is a less valid specialty than \u201c8% of the time this Ability comes up,\u201d yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T17:05:13-07:00","id":1414670,"title":"","content":"Honestly, one of the reasons why I've moved towards not really liking how Exalted handles specialties is because they all cost the same, but trying to make them all worth the same is basically impossible. While experience and system mastery can help a lot in getting it right, it's impossible to ever really know if a given specialty is going to come up so much it's basically another dot in the Ability, or if you're lucky it ever matters.<br /> <br /> What's a good balance between too often and not often enough isn't something players can reasonably predict ahead of time... so why ask them to try?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T14:30:15-07:00","id":1414817,"title":"","content":"I made a character with Integrity (No Time For Your Bullshit). The idea is that he gets the bonus when somebody tries to distract or sidetrack him with irrelevancies and/or trivia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T08:54:38-07:00","id":1414923,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Realised I'd unhelpfully proposed stuff others had already suggested. Deleted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1414817#post1414817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a character with Integrity (No Time For Your Bullshit). The idea is that he gets the bonus when somebody tries to distract or sidetrack him with irrelevancies and/or trivia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I find Integrity specialties one of the hardest to come up with characterful ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 09-21-2020, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T17:08:04-07:00","id":1415247,"title":"","content":"I made a thread in ages past about this very topic as it relates to Melee (Brawl/Archery/MA/etc) <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too\"> I hate Melee Specialties (and you should too) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222772-i-hate-melee-specialties-and-you-should-too </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Provocative title out of the way, I hate the way Melee Specialties are boring flat bonuses. Lets posit a few statements first: 1- Only one specialty applies at a </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry i cant format it I'm mobile at the moment. <br /> <br /> Basically, i find it incredibly bad design that the game says &quot;your specialty shouldn't always apply&quot; and &quot;Melee (Swords) is fine&quot;. Many exalted take an artifact right out of the gate and if not they usually find one early enough. Call the Blade shuts down disarming (and honestly, how often does Disarming come up?) And TTRPGs just can't replicate the videogame feel of switching weapons for different combat scenarios. <br /> <br /> So I told my players to think of an interesting specialty and that their weapons weren't allowed. Here's what they did: <br /> <br /> Melee: Sword Tricks. This is functionally a specialty in Stunts but the player is new to rpgs and pretty hesitant to express himself. So his character used to do sword tricks on the street for money to finance his Occult studies in exorcism, and it really incentivizes him to RP more. As much as the conventional wisdom is &quot;stunt every attack&quot; it only comes up on the 2 pointers, so it works out. <br /> <br /> Brawl: Grapple. Toes the line, but I allowed it. It doesnt help any of the punching or kicking and the player only uses Brawl as a side piece to Single Point, which leads to<br /> <br /> Single Point: On a Boat. He's a pirate. This is exactly the kind of specialty i wanted to see because its cool, it reinforces the RP of the character, and its not always on. Its probably 50/50 in our campain so far. <br /> <br /> Integrity: Heresy. Self explanatory and awesome. <br /> <br /> Melee: Against Artifact Users. This is mine on my crafter. He is an artifact weapon and armor smith, so using an artifact against him gives him a ton of insight into your fighting style. Only comes up against other Exalt mostly but thats enough for a non primary combatant. <br /> <br /> Ebon Shadow: Dynasts. An assassin with a specific type, hes studied DBs enough to know how they think and how their powers work. Also its implied that the specialty is 50-99% his raw hatred for them pushing him on. <br /> <br /> Occult: Ghosts and Occult: Demons. Two different characters. Serviceable, a little boring but they belong to an Exorcist and a Demonologist respectively so it reinforces what they are good at. This and Lore are pretty much Carte Blanche to pick something boring but practical<br /> <br /> Lore: Military, Lore: Great Houses, Lore: First Age. Pretty standard. <br /> <br /> Stealth: (setting up an) Ambush. This one is interesting because it doesn't cover thievery and spying, but it does cover anything related to murder. Its powerful, sure, but it has a strong theme and doesn't cover the out of combat uses for stealth (which is a lot of the table time)<br /> <br /> I'll stop there. One thing i wanted to show is that specialties in Emotional reasons can be quite interesting (i.e. Hate based specialties pushing you to succeed), and good specialties should reinforce your character's role play (the pirate at sea), and sometimes, just sometimes, boring is fine (Lore and Occult)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T00:39:52-07:00","id":1415272,"title":"","content":"Reading you I realize I'm not a fan of the fact that specialties apply only to one ability. Like, Single Point : On a Boat for the Pirate. Let the guy just have On a Boat as a generic specialty that apply for most concerned abilities when he's on a boat, and be done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T04:26:44-07:00","id":1415288,"title":"","content":"I really don't think speciaIties are a big enough deal to warrant a bunch of hand-wringing so I like them by the book. Dodge (Evasion) and Melee (Swords) are both fine.<br /> <br /> Also compared to raising an Ability, specialties are actually pretty costly so if you start limiting them much more they're just a waste of xp on any ability that isn't already at 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 09-24-2020, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T06:27:42-07:00","id":1415293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415288#post1415288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't think speciaIties are a big enough deal to warrant a bunch of hand-wringing so I like them by the book. Dodge (Evasion) and Melee (Swords) are both fine.<br /> <br /> Also compared to raising an Ability, specialties are actually pretty costly so if you start limiting them much more they're just a waste of xp on any ability that isn't already at 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just makes them a free dot since you get 4 at chargen. Everyone is gonna put 1 in offense and 1 in defense and then its a wash. Its boring. Its a non system.<br /> <br /> Also what is Dodge (Evasion)? Every Dodge is an evasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T06:40:10-07:00","id":1415295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415293#post1415293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also what is Dodge (Evasion)? Every Dodge is an evasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s Capital-E Evasion. You can also roll Dodge to Disengage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T08:12:54-07:00","id":1415298,"title":"","content":"My stance on Melee ([Weapon Type]) is... Well it <i>is</i> at least minimally flavorful and <i>does</i> technically have a firmly defined opportunity cost, which is enough for me to find it hard to find it objectionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T08:13:28-07:00","id":1415299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415295#post1415295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s Capital-E Evasion. You can also roll Dodge to Disengage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to avoid environmental hazards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T08:46:57-07:00","id":1415300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415272#post1415272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading you I realize I'm not a fan of the fact that specialties apply only to one ability. Like, Single Point : On a Boat for the Pirate. Let the guy just have On a Boat as a generic specialty that apply for most concerned abilities when he's on a boat, and be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way they do specialties in the Trinity version of the Storypath system. Being really good at something gives you a bonus to other rolls related to that thing. So, if you are really good at fighting with swords, you get a bonus to craft swords or know the lore of a sword. Or, if you're really good at fixing cars, you get a bonus to drive them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T08:52:05-07:00","id":1415301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415300#post1415300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the way they do specialties in the Trinity version of the Storypath system. Being really good at something gives you a bonus to other rolls related to that thing. So, if you are really good at fighting with swords, you get a bonus to craft swords or know the lore of a sword. Or, if you're really good at fixing cars, you get a bonus to drive them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes much more sense to me than the &quot;specialty per ability&quot; currently in charge, and seems much more fluid and interesting for the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T10:02:20-07:00","id":1415303,"title":"","content":"Interdisciplinary Specialty is a merit in CofD, could always crib that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T15:08:17-07:00","id":1415327,"title":"","content":"The Storypath approach is probably more satisfying for Exalted than the CofD approach. One of the reasons is that the bonuses specialties apply in Storypath are asymmetrical. While the different Storypath games don't use the same implementations, the boost to when your specialty applies to other Skills is usually more direct.<br /> <br /> An off-the-cuff example of the Storypath approach translated to Exalted:<br /> <br /> When a specialty applies to a roll with the Ability it is attached to, regain 1 WP if the roll fails (can't exceed your max), if the specialty applies to the roll of another Ability, gain +1 success.<br /> <br /> So if you have Melee (Swords) instead of a +1 to your Melee pools when using swords, the big bonus is if you're fighting a tough opponent you're more free to bust out WP without tapping yourself dry. If you're rolling Read Intentions action while watching two people have a sword duel (or even against an opponent you're fighting if you're good enough to spare time for that), your expertise in sword fighting gives you a bonus success to see how emotions are fueling tactical choices. <br /> <br /> That said, this does throw people off a bit at first because they're used to specialty = eke out some bonuses in a sub-set of applications of an Ability, and it having no increase in your maximum talent with its primary source can feel weird. But IME that's mostly a learned jargon issue than a fun/mechanical issue.<br /> <br /> For me the two big advantages of this approach are:<br /> <br /> 1) Creating a natural sense of broad competence without feeling like you have to invest a bunch of dots in Abilities just because they'd make sense for your character to have some training in to go along with the Abilities you focus on.<br /> <br /> 2) The &quot;Boring but practical&quot; vs, &quot;Awesome but impractical,&quot; divide is lessened. Specialties need to make sense as things that would apply to actions from multiple Abilities, so anything that's too focused on boosting a specific mechanic that relies on an Ability is less valuable. This applies to highly technical specialties like Awareness (Join Battle) or flavorful but overly specific ones like Resistance (Enduring Extreme Heat while Naked and Unarmed). If you find yourself really stretching to apply these to other Abilities, they're no good. By encouraging players to get creative with their specialties, they're less likely to end up with &quot;wasted&quot; picks that never come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T20:04:42-07:00","id":1415358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415298#post1415298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My stance on Melee ([Weapon Type]) is... Well it <i>is</i> at least minimally flavorful and <i>does</i> technically have a firmly defined opportunity cost, which is enough for me to find it hard to find it objectionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im really iffy on the opportunity cost bit because their is no inventive to ever switch weapons on your primary combat ability (Sword to Axe). Sure you could pull out a bow (and get the bow specialty), but its not like Exalted has the same weapons-and-scenarios system that Devil May Cry, Bastion, or any other multiweapon combat action rpg has. There's no feeling like &quot;this room is full of fast moving weak knife spammers. Better switch from Axe to Spear for the wide area attacks&quot;. <br /> <br /> Its a really small point, we're talking about a single die here, but I just think its more fun to come up with a cool scenario than a freebie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T22:18:53-07:00","id":1415365,"title":"","content":"To the contrary - switching from one weapon to another can potentially give you two extra Accuracy dice or even a point of Defense. Switching out to better fit the circumstances is very reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T22:45:30-07:00","id":1415366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415365#post1415365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the contrary - switching from one weapon to another can potentially give you two extra Accuracy dice or even a point of Defense. Switching out to better fit the circumstances is very reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, although there exits swords of all three size categories, and with the tags Balanced, Chopping, Disarming, Reaching, Two-Handed and I believe piercing although I can't find the stats for the artifact rapier.<br /> <br /> I very much encourage people who don't take artifact weapons, especially for characters who are fighty warrior types to think about taking a variety of weapons, but it doesn't much help that one specialty can cover so many. Flexible is really the only awesome tag that you don't get from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T02:28:18-07:00","id":1415376,"title":"","content":"You have a Specialty in swords. I attack you with a foe using a Grimcleaver. You kill them/they flee leaving their weapon behind/you disarm them. If you aren't even tempted by that Grimcleaver then I've failed as an ST, because I should have narrated how amazing it is and what an awesome treasure has fallen into your lap.<br /> <br /> What if you're disarmed?<br /> What about a bar fight?<br /> What if your foe is warded against swords?<br /> Or has acid blood which can be avoided if you bludgeon them?<br /> Or a liche breaks your ancestral sword in two?<br /> Or you're forced into a gladitorial arena?<br /> Or challenged to a ritualistic knife fight?<br /> <br /> Melee (swords) should apply 90-95% of the time. But once every twenty sessions it's on the ST to think of something interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-25-2020, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T03:50:29-07:00","id":1415391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415376#post1415376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a Specialty in swords. I attack you with a foe using a Grimcleaver. You kill them/they flee leaving their weapon behind/you disarm them. If you aren't even tempted by that Grimcleaver then I've failed as an ST, because I should have narrated how amazing it is and what an awesome treasure has fallen into your lap.<br /> <br /> What if you're disarmed?<br /> What about a bar fight?<br /> What if your foe is warded aagainst swords?<br /> Or has acid blood which can be avoided if you bludgeon them?<br /> Or a liche breaks your ancestral sword in two?<br /> Or you're forced into a gladitorial arena?<br /> Or challenged to a ritualistic knife fight?<br /> <br /> Melee (swords) should apply 90-95% of the time. But once every twenty sessions it's on the ST to think of something interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The setting and the characters in Exalted are already totally overloaded in scenaristic and gameplay hook honestly. I don't think specialties do a good job of adding more. An Artifact sword would pull up Ann your interesting hooks (albeit the one about breaking the sword, and I'm pretty sure something can be made to work around that), and I think it's much better integrated to the fiction and to the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T17:26:47-07:00","id":1415482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415376#post1415376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a Specialty in swords. I attack you with a foe using a Grimcleaver. You kill them/they flee leaving their weapon behind/you disarm them. If you aren't even tempted by that Grimcleaver then I've failed as an ST, because I should have narrated how amazing it is and what an awesome treasure has fallen into your lap.<br /> <br /> What if you're disarmed?<br /> What about a bar fight?<br /> What if your foe is warded against swords?<br /> Or has acid blood which can be avoided if you bludgeon them?<br /> Or a liche breaks your ancestral sword in two?<br /> Or you're forced into a gladitorial arena?<br /> Or challenged to a ritualistic knife fight?<br /> <br /> Melee (swords) should apply 90-95% of the time. But once every twenty sessions it's on the ST to think of something interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take your point but I don't really like these. If i take Melee (Swords) at your table and the ST says &quot;I bet it would be cool to give him an Artifact Axe just because he doesn't have a specialty in it&quot;, that's not really good game design unless the player wants to be forced to experiment. And it doesn't prevent the problem that most (i'm seriously guessing over half) of players <i>start</i> with an artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> Disarmed: I never see this, it requires a successful gambit, and its stopped by stunts and Call The Blade.<br /> Bar Fight: Its probably just for fun and if lethal weapons come out, so does my glorious solar nailbat<br /> Warded Against Swords: The <b>Nuclear Fuck You</b> option of RPGs. Presumably the other Solars can still kill this guy while you take on the mooks.<br /> Acid Blood: Stunt with the flat of the blade<br /> Litch: almost certainly can't break an artifact. If he breaks my ancestral mundane sword im gonna use the hilt like a knife.<br /> Gladiatorial Arena: No one short of a Deathlord has the power to force Solars into an arena against their choice. Even then, it doesn't stop Call The Blade<br /> Ritual Knife fight: cool. I like that one, it makes sense. But no other specialty matters here anyway<br /> <br /> These scenarios seem like a real stretch/bend over backward just to say &quot;You don't <i>always</i> get the Melee (Swords) bonus&quot;. Even then, no other specialty would cover these anyway unless you had Melee (Acid Blooded Knife Fighting Litch Gladiator Bar Fights) which admittedly, <u><i><b>is the coolest specialty of all time</b></i></u>.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm sticking with my point: Melee (Swords) is boring. It's poorly designed. Starting with an artifact and taking one of the coolest charms in the game prevents 99% of scenarios where it wouldn't come up. My houserule to ban it might not match everyone's table, but its given me MA (On a Boat), Melee (In a Storm), Melee (Sword Tricks), MA (Dyansts), Melee (Artifact Users), Melee (Outnumbered) Melee (With My Grandmothers' Ghosts) and Melee (Bodyguarding), which I think are more fun to play with.<br /> <br /> But this is an extremely minor, 1 dice effect and i doubt it really matters. as always, YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T22:35:45-07:00","id":1415509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415482#post1415482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These scenarios seem like a real stretch/bend over backward just to say &quot;You don't <i>always</i> get the Melee (Swords) bonus&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that melee(swords) feels too broad for a real specialty, but part of this is on the Storyteller. Like how if you have a specialty in occult(ghosts) they're kind of obligated to include ghosts at some point, unless you've talked to them and they're fully aware that specialty will go wasted. Samewise, if you have a specialty it's perfectly reasonable for something kind of unlikely to happen that disarms that specialty, or even your whole primary combat ability in general.<br /> <br /> Like maybe the owner of the gladatorial arena has some info you need, and will grant one request to the winner, but there's stipulations like no outside weapons. Or if you're a Solar just as likely you don't want to instantly flag yourself as somebody the Wyld Hunt should investigate. So you for those series of fights you need to use whatever they give you to use, which may include a lot of non-sword weapons.<br /> <br /> Maybe one round even consists of barehanded fighting and you have to get by on whatever dots of Brawl you bought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T01:42:07-07:00","id":1415515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1414267-how-do-you-like-your-specialties?p=1415482#post1415482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take your point but I don't really like these. If i take Melee (Swords) at your table and the ST says &quot;I bet it would be cool to give him an Artifact Axe just because he doesn't have a specialty in it&quot;, that's not really good game design unless the player wants to be forced to experiment. And it doesn't prevent the problem that most (i'm seriously guessing over half) of players <i>start</i> with an artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> Disarmed: I never see this, it requires a successful gambit, and its stopped by stunts and Call The Blade.<br /> Bar Fight: Its probably just for fun and if lethal weapons come out, so does my glorious solar nailbat<br /> Warded Against Swords: The <b>Nuclear Fuck You</b> option of RPGs. Presumably the other Solars can still kill this guy while you take on the mooks.<br /> Acid Blood: Stunt with the flat of the blade<br /> Litch: almost certainly can't break an artifact. If he breaks my ancestral mundane sword im gonna use the hilt like a knife.<br /> Gladiatorial Arena: No one short of a Deathlord has the power to force Solars into an arena against their choice. Even then, it doesn't stop Call The Blade<br /> Ritual Knife fight: cool. I like that one, it makes sense. But no other specialty matters here anyway<br /> <br /> These scenarios seem like a real stretch/bend over backward just to say &quot;You don't <i>always</i> get the Melee (Swords) bonus&quot;. Even then, no other specialty would cover these anyway unless you had Melee (Acid Blooded Knife Fighting Litch Gladiator Bar Fights) which admittedly, <u><i><b>is the coolest specialty of all time</b></i></u>.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm sticking with my point: Melee (Swords) is boring. It's poorly designed. Starting with an artifact and taking one of the coolest charms in the game prevents 99% of scenarios where it wouldn't come up. My houserule to ban it might not match everyone's table, but its given me MA (On a Boat), Melee (In a Storm), Melee (Sword Tricks), MA (Dyansts), Melee (Artifact Users), Melee (Outnumbered) Melee (With My Grandmothers' Ghosts) and Melee (Bodyguarding), which I think are more fun to play with.<br /> <br /> But this is an extremely minor, 1 dice effect and i doubt it really matters. as always, YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to justify every off-the-cuff story idea I have. But I will address this:<br /> <br /> Disarmed: You're still forcing mote expenditure or a flurry on Draw/Ready. Disarm is a great tactic for NPCs who will usually roll enough Initiative to open with it as a Gambit, or who can have Charms to enhance. It's rarely &quot;worth it&quot; for a PC fighting optimized opponents to the death... but It's great for drama.<br /> <br /> Bar Fight: You can wield a chair leg (or a pewter mug or glass bottle) with Melee as an Improvised weapon without the immediate lethal escalation of drawing a sword. (Or falling back on your Brawl 0.)<br /> <br /> Acid blood: Sure you can Stunt. But I'm calling the flat of your blade an Improvised weapon and I'm saying your Specialty still doesn't apply.<br /> <br /> Litch: Shattering Fist Strike lets Dragon-Blooded break artifact weapons. I'm not saying your sword is gone forever, but there is massive scope for &quot;this powerful opponent renders your main weapon unusable&quot;. Heck, Black Claw Style is right there.<br /> <br /> Gladiator fight: A gang of mortals with pointy sticks can take down a Solar. You lose attunement to your artifacts after one day of being apart from them. You absolutely can be beaten down to Incap and wake up without your weapons in an arena. Or, you know, enter for fun -- fame, coin and glory. Or as the Dr suggests, maybe the arena owner has something you want.<br /> <br /> Ritual knife fight: A specialty of &quot;single opponents&quot; or &quot;acrobatics&quot; or &quot;defending my honor&quot; or &quot;knives&quot; or &quot;ritual combat&quot; or &quot;playing to an audience&quot; or &quot;dirty fighting&quot; or &quot;whilst wounded&quot; might apply.<br /> <br /> Ward Vs Swords: When playing Exalted, sometimes you need to go nuclear. Not always. The Exalted kick ass and should feel kick ass. But I'm saying challenge the PCs once every 20 sessions. I can easily see a Fae Swordwizard whose entire court is immune to swords. Or a Second Circle Demon with complete immunity surrounded by First Circles with partial immunity. Or a single boss monster with no mooks -- The Behemoth of Blades.<br /> <br /> And even if you already have Shining Ice Mirror... if I throw an axe that lets you breath underwater fight before you have to confront Leviathan, or a lance that makes you immune to fire as you march on Gem, that should provoke an interesting choice -- do you play to your strengths or shore up your weaknesses?<br /> <br /> But yes, my point is that your Specialty SHOULD nearly always apply. It should be a contrivance to put the players on the backfoot.<br /> <br /> IRL, I am not good at dancing. So I don't enter a dance competition every week. My RPG characters who are not good at dancing, likewise should not be forced into a dance competition every week. But as a deliberate contrivance, it works as a one-off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-26-2020, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T08:03:20-07:00","id":1415539,"title":"","content":"I still go off the 1E developer comment that specialties should probably apply most of the time. But there's a pretty big difference between 60% and 99%, and that seems to be where the Melee: Swords argument lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T13:52:23-07:00","id":1415593,"title":"","content":"I think there's also another axis besides levels frequency:<br /> <br /> I feel like some people want specialties to come up a lot because players are being creative: coming up with neat ways to apply specialties that seem more narrow, trying to manipulate events into ones that favor their edge, etc.<br /> <br /> I feel like some people (and could easily be overlapping) want specialties to come up a lot because it ensures a player investment is worth it, but to the value of the investment means it shouldn't come up every time.<br /> <br /> I don't think the current rules actually support either group that well. The first is hamstrung a bit by how minor a bonus they are (except for DBs) for the effort of encouraging them to come up be on the players more than the ST. The second is hampered by the creation of a more antagonistic player vs. ST mentality of the ST needing to introduce situations to make specialties apply less than 100% of the time (however much the &quot;right&quot; % is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}